IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-wreck-stores`
IMPORT `ccc13-tests-support`

-- ccc13-tests-wreck-stores.l4 -- tests of ccc13-wreck-stores.l4 (ss 415 to 421). Expected values are decided from the text.

`ccc13 test the hybrid class` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
GIVETH A `s 2 wreck kind`
`ccc13 test wreck` MEANS `the cargo of a vessel`
GIVETH A `s 2 wreck kind`
`ccc13 test not wreck` MEANS `a thing that is none of those`
GIVETH A `s 2 representative: the person's place in the organization`
`ccc13 test a representative` MEANS `a director of the organization`
GIVETH A `s 2 representative: the person's place in the organization`
`ccc13 test not a representative` MEANS `a person who is none of those in respect of the organization`

§ `s 415 wreck`
-- inputs of (a): what the thing is; secretes, defaces or conceals; from a person entitled to inquire
#ASSERT `s 415(a) the conduct is the offence of concealing wreck` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 415(a) the conduct is the offence of concealing wreck` `ccc13 test wreck` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 415(a) the conduct is the offence of concealing wreck` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 415(a) the conduct is the offence of concealing wreck` `ccc13 test not wreck` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- s 2 wreck "includes": a thing outside its list is not covered
-- inputs of (b): what the thing is; receives wreck knowing it is wreck from a person other than the owner or a receiver; hours since receipt; hours after receipt at which the receiver was informed
#ASSERT `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE 49 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE         -- more than forty-eight hours and the receiver not informed
#ASSERT `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE 48 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- exactly forty-eight hours: still "within forty-eight hours"
#ASSERT `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE 100 (JUST 48) EQUALS JUST FALSE       -- informed at exactly forty-eight hours: within
#ASSERT `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE 100 (JUST 48.5) EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- informed after forty-eight hours
#ASSERT `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE 100 (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `ccc13 test wreck` FALSE 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- did not receive it from such a person
#ASSERT `s 415(b) the conduct is the offence of receiving wreck and not informing the receiver` `ccc13 test not wreck` TRUE 100 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 415(c) the conduct is the offence of dealing with wreck without lawful authority` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 415(c) the conduct is the offence of dealing with wreck without lawful authority` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE       -- with lawful authority
#ASSERT `s 415(c) the conduct is the offence of dealing with wreck without lawful authority` `ccc13 test wreck` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 415(c) the conduct is the offence of dealing with wreck without lawful authority` `ccc13 test not wreck` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 415(d) the conduct is the offence of keeping wreck` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 415(d) the conduct is the offence of keeping wreck` `ccc13 test wreck` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- not longer than the time reasonably necessary to deliver it
#ASSERT `s 415(d) the conduct is the offence of keeping wreck` `ccc13 test wreck` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 415(e) the conduct is the offence of boarding a wrecked vessel` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 415(e) the conduct is the offence of boarding a wrecked vessel` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "unless he is a receiver of wreck or a person acting under orders of a receiver of wreck"
#ASSERT `s 415(e) the conduct is the offence of boarding a wrecked vessel` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 415 the person is guilty of an offence in relation to wreck` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 415 the person is guilty of an offence in relation to wreck` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 415 the person is guilty of an offence in relation to wreck` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 415 the person is guilty of an offence in relation to wreck` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 415 the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
#ASSERT `s 415 the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`

§ `s 417 public stores`
#ASSERT `s 417(3) the mark is a distinguishing mark` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 417(3) the mark is a distinguishing mark` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inputs of (1): without lawful authority; applies the mark; intent to conceal Her Majesty's property in public stores; removes or obliterates the mark; the mark is a distinguishing mark (s 417(3))
#ASSERT `s 417(1) the conduct is the offence of applying or removing a distinguishing mark` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 417(1) the conduct is the offence of applying or removing a distinguishing mark` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 417(1) the conduct is the offence of applying or removing a distinguishing mark` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- (a) needs the absence of lawful authority
#ASSERT `s 417(1) the conduct is the offence of applying or removing a distinguishing mark` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- (b) needs the removal as well as the intent
#ASSERT `s 417(1) the conduct is the offence of applying or removing a distinguishing mark` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- not a distinguishing mark
#ASSERT `s 417(1) the conduct is the offence of applying or removing a distinguishing mark` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 417(1) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
#ASSERT `s 417(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
-- inputs of (2): without lawful authority; receives, possesses, keeps, sells or delivers; the stores are personal property; under the care of a public department; knows they bear a distinguishing mark; the mark (s 417(3))
#ASSERT `s 417(2) the conduct is the offence of unlawful transactions in public stores` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 417(2) the conduct is the offence of unlawful transactions in public stores` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 417(2) the conduct is the offence of unlawful transactions in public stores` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- does not know the stores bear the mark
#ASSERT `s 417(2) the conduct is the offence of unlawful transactions in public stores` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING        -- s 2 public stores "includes": not under a public department's care is not covered
#ASSERT `s 417(2) the conduct is the offence of unlawful transactions in public stores` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 417(2) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
#ASSERT `s 417(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
#ASSERT `s 418(1) the conduct is the offence of selling defective stores to Her Majesty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 418(1) the conduct is the offence of selling defective stores to Her Majesty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 418(1) the conduct is the offence of selling defective stores to Her Majesty` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 418(1) the punishments`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the number of limbs` (`s 418(1) the punishments`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 418(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
-- inputs of (2): the person's place in the organization (s 2 representative); the body is an organization (s 2); the organization commits fraud under (1); (a) takes part; (b) knows or suspects; informs the government
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` `ccc13 test a representative` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` `ccc13 test a representative` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- (b): knew and did not inform
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` `ccc13 test a representative` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE       -- (b): informed the government
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` `ccc13 test a representative` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` `ccc13 test a representative` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- the organization did not commit the offence
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` `ccc13 test not a representative` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the conduct is the offence of a representative of an organization taking part in fraud on Her Majesty` `ccc13 test a representative` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 418(2) the punishments`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
#ASSERT `s 418(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`

§ `s 419 to s 421 military uniforms, stores and evidence`
-- inputs of 419: without lawful authority; (a) wears a uniform; (b) wears a mark or medal; (c) possesses a certificate not issued to them; (d) possesses an altered commission or certificate
#ASSERT `s 419 the conduct is the offence of unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 419 the conduct is the offence of unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 419 the conduct is the offence of unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 419 the conduct is the offence of unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 419 the conduct is the offence of unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- with lawful authority
#ASSERT `s 419 the conduct is the offence of unlawful use of military uniforms or certificates` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the number of limbs` (`s 419 the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 419 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 420(2) the person is saved from conviction of an offence under section 420` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 420(2) the person is saved from conviction of an offence under section 420` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inputs of 420(1): buys, receives or detains from a member, deserter or absentee; the stores are Her Majesty's or accountable to her; the defence of (2)
#ASSERT `s 420(1) the conduct is the offence of buying military stores` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 420(1) the conduct is the offence of buying military stores` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- did not know and had no reason to suspect
#ASSERT `s 420(1) the conduct is the offence of buying military stores` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 420(1) the conduct is the offence of buying military stores` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 420(1) the conduct is the offence of buying military stores` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 420(1) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
#ASSERT `s 420(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
#ASSERT `s 421(1) the evidence is proof that the person's enrolment in the Canadian Forces prior to that time was regular` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 421(1) the evidence is proof that the person's enrolment in the Canadian Forces prior to that time was regular` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 421(1) the evidence is proof that the person's enrolment in the Canadian Forces prior to that time was regular` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 421(1) the evidence is proof that the person's enrolment in the Canadian Forces prior to that time was regular` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 421(2) the accused is presumed to have known that the stores bore a distinguishing mark` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 421(2) the accused is presumed to have known that the stores bore a distinguishing mark` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 421(2) the accused is presumed to have known that the stores bore a distinguishing mark` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 421(2) the accused is presumed to have known that the stores bore a distinguishing mark` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
